      {
        "text": "# QA Follow-Up Review — Grok 4.6 ARENA-SIX-20260919 (Round 2)\n\n**Reviewer:** qa-redteam (isolated, advisory) · **Session/lane:** `arena-six-grok46-followup-qa-20260919` · **Mode:** read-only; no reruns, no edits, no config/runtime/authority changes · **Date:** 2026-09-19\n\n## Scope\n\nRead-only verification of all 15 artifacts listed in `manifest.json` under `arena-six-grok46-review2-20260919/`: manifest, report, run-contract, operational-adjudication, failure-taxonomy, terminal-receipts (20 rows), graded-results, incumbent-comparison, validation, keys, t4-tool-traces, t4-transcript-evidence, grader.py, candidate-turns (20 rows), envelope, gateway-canary. Scores were independently recalculated from `candidate-turns.json` visible text against `keys.json` using the declared grader contract.\n\n## Findings\n\n**Critical:** None.\n\n**High:** None.\n\n**Medium:**\n- **M-A — Incumbent baseline unverifiable from this packet.** `incumbent-comparison.json` is a projection quoting `source_sha256` of `../incumbent-baseline-20260919/graded-results.json` and an embedded `source_main_acceptance` record; the underlying source file is outside the packet, so the incumbent figures (GLM 8 strict/11 eligible, DeepSeek 8 strict/12) cannot be independently re-verified here. All comparison claims are *internally consistent* with the projection and with `validation.json`, but they rest on an unverified external hash. Recommend Main spot-check the source hash once.\n- **M-B — Unsupported report claim.** `report.md` says \"keep its existing Research Scout assignment,\" but no artifact in the packet evidences any existing Grok assignment. Advisory-only claim; does not affect scores or the no-promotion boundary.\n\n**Low:**\n- **L-A — T4 repetition asymmetry (disclosed).** R1 invoked the missing `primary.json` with `optional:false` (hard tool error, `tool_summary_failures:1`); R2 used `optional:true` (structured not-found). Both followed the identical four-read path, stayed within budget, no forbidden reads, no score impact. Flagged in `t4-tool-traces.json` `failure_counter_note`; acceptable.\n- **L-B — Mixed strict denominator for GLM in the report table.** Strict cell reads `8/12` (planned) while GLM had 11 operationally eligible; eligibility is disclosed in adjacent cells, so a skimming reader could misread 8/11 as 8/12-eligible. Cosmetic.\n- **L-C — Canary payload includes token/cost usage** (`costUsd` 0.0286) while the report declares cost out of scope. Not scored; no impact.\n\n## Score Verdict — Confirmed\n\nIndependent recalculation from raw turns + keys confirms all claimed scores and failure classifications:\n\n| Dimension | Claimed | Recalculated | Verified failures |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| Strict | 9/12 | **9/12** | T2-r2 (A.status `blocked` vs frozen `queued`), T4-r2 (visible narration before tools), T5-r2 (extra `W1:false` in `approvals`) |\n| Factual | 10/12 | **10/12** | T2-r2, T5-r2 |\n| Full-interaction format | 11/12 | **11/12** | T4-r2 only |\n| Tools | 12/12 | **12/12** | none; both T4 reps used exactly 4 permitted reads, no forbidden archive |\n\n- **Transport integrity:** all **20/20** terminal receipts show `requested` = `xai/grok-4.6`, `effective` provider xai / model grok-4.6 / responseModel grok-4.6, `identity_valid:true`, `fallback_used:false`, `rerouted:false`, single-attempt execution traces. Zero reroute/fallback/timeout/parse failure. Duration stats (min 19.867 / max 332.117) match turn-level elapsed data.\n- **Incumbent claims:** GLM T1 0/2 and DeepSeek T1 1/2 vs Grok 2/2 confirmed; DeepSeek factual 10/12 tie confirmed; GLM format 11/11-eligible vs Grok 11/12 correctly denominator-qualified in the report; repeated-strict families 3/6 for all three models confirmed.\n- **Promotion language:** `report.md` explicitly states the result \"does **not** authorize a routing or configuration change,\" \"Do not promote it into other roles from this result alone,\" and \"two repetitions per family are consistency evidence, not a reliability estimate.\" No automatic-promotion implication found.\n\n## Prior-Finding Resolution\n\n| Round-1 finding | Claimed fix | Verified state |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 (incumbent comparison missing) | comparison file + full validation summary added | **Resolved with limit** — added and internally consistent; external source hash unverifiable from packet (see M-A) |\n| M2 (run contract / evidence root) | run-contract + result-root projections; report clarifies root | **Resolved** — run-contract present; report declares result directory authoritative |\n| L1 (taxonomy scoring fields) | scoring_dimension / scoring_rule added | **Resolved** — present on all 3 failures |\n| L2 (T4 visible-stream evidence) | t4-transcript-evidence.json added | **Resolved** — per-turn visible narration + tool calls present |\n| L3 (scoring contract) | graded-results scoring_contract added | **Resolved** — two-layer contract explicit and matches applied grading |\n| Receipt limit (10/20 receipts) | all 20 receipts included | **Resolved** — 20/20 verified |\n\n## Proof Limits\n\n- File `sha256` values in `manifest.json` were not recomputed (no exec); hashes taken as declared.\n- Incumbent baseline source and main-acceptance record exist only as quoted projections inside this packet.\n- `report.md` evidence links (`independent-qa-review.json`, `matrix-index.json`, `attempts/`) point to the result root, not the packet; root-link integrity not verified here.\n- Two repetitions per family = consistency evidence, not reliability, as the packet itself states.\n- Provider usage for this QA turn: `provider_usage_unavailable` (read-only tool calls; no token/cost counters exposed to this agent).\n\n## Final Verdict\n\n**PASS** — all round-one findings addressed; scores (9/12 strict, 10/12 factual, 11/12 format, 12/12 tools), all three failure classifications, 20/20 transport receipts, and incumbent comparison claims verified as internally consistent; no promotion implication in `report.md`.\n\n**Main acceptance recommendation:** Accept with limits — pending one optional Main spot-check of the `incumbent-baseline-20260919` source hash (M-A) and the unevidenced \"Research Scout assignment\" phrasing (M-B). No rework lane required; this verdict is advisory and unaccepted until Main verifies.",
